{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:30:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_fc7daaf917a34b80b4790f6c97eb113e","id":"pg_6105835a8ab5526ab5a92bfd3ac4568f","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/patched-codes-patchwork-code-of-conduct-md-21948cbec44d-2bfd3ac4568f.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_a2d23c08e5a75e02a1fe91accb4a088e"],"title":"patched-codes/patchwork/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md @ 21948cbec44d","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:30:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fc7daaf917a34b80b4790f6c97eb113e"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_1bbaba8205ee9df325123990282e47b1a15eb3e5527976716f1c00364c56160f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Optional pip dependency groups exist: 'security' (semgrep, depscan) required for AutoFix and DependencyUpgrade, 'rag' (chromadb) required for ResolveIssue, 'notifications' for notification steps, and 'all' which installs everything."},{"claim_ids":["clm_507a34e5525d06859c2507d4f1deaee89f176d0a63b70e3be9c8035475eb795d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Patchwork appears relevant to security automation use cases, since its AutoFix patchflow patches vulnerabilities identified by Semgrep scans and DependencyUpgrade updates dependencies from vulnerable to fixed versions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_686d0ae78a78b7abfa03495ae02af2d265d48d1fa0bd948217215401a41acff4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributions for new patchflows, steps, or the core framework are welcomed, with separate instruction documents for creating patchflows and steps, plus a HuggingChat assistant to help author them."},{"claim_ids":["clm_72b06c24e0f4a56797a3f1bd8e0e1589b98d7c34e9000f89a1c1714bd239a5fa"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Patchflow configuration can be supplied via a --config flag pointing to a directory of patchflow defaults or to a config.yml file specifying keys such as openai_api_key, client_base_url, and model."},{"claim_ids":["clm_75f6254c08b372942de2c68bb5b36429cb3889e0702246025a87d606ae2d89fc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Predefined patchflows include GenerateDocstring, AutoFix, PRReview, GenerateREADME, DependencyUpgrade, and ResolveIssue, each linked to its own directory in the repository."},{"claim_ids":["clm_802ca562c52decf5f6155c4b3b52df561ea956d672a7b2205962c5aec10351fe"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Installing patchwork-cli without any dependency group installs a core set of dependencies sufficient to run the GenerateDocstring, PRReview, and GenerateREADME patchflows."},{"claim_ids":["clm_bcfb9b614523b974f2dc868d667ecd693f46fa6660ac174d75cde8ed6334078c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Patchwork supports any OpenAI-compatible endpoint, enabling models from providers like Groq, Together AI, or Hugging Face, and local models via llama.cpp, ollama, vllm, or tgi."},{"claim_ids":["clm_eb9b3d058152902a155c12a496f1b71be8082f6ae154e12501d250edcf0aa543"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Patchwork is licensed under AGPL-3.0 terms, while the separate patchwork template repository for creating and sharing custom patchflows and steps is licensed under Apache-2.0."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f3c7c5b3e09dce8e228ddd65d370a6c1f9e3aaf2ad8139393c5482b1f24fc103"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Patchwork is built from three key components: reusable atomic steps (e.g., create PR, commit changes, call an LLM), customizable prompt templates, and patchflows that combine steps and prompts into automations."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fabbbf3f4b19050237a43e34da3c6ffe92e35dba3c9f299ca5e1ec2c4331fb3e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI runs patchflows with the syntax 'patchwork <PatchFlow> <?Arguments>'; arguments override patchflow attributes as key=value pairs, and valueless keys are treated as boolean True flags."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fd5514cb5bb578c53202434fd7f5d4a9fd1f940ecfd2d9489b350c8335be030b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Prompt templates use {{}} placeholder variables replaced at each run with data from steps or inputs; each patchflow ships with an optimized default template that users can override via prompt_template_file."}],"claim_ids":["clm_1bbaba8205ee9df325123990282e47b1a15eb3e5527976716f1c00364c56160f","clm_507a34e5525d06859c2507d4f1deaee89f176d0a63b70e3be9c8035475eb795d","clm_686d0ae78a78b7abfa03495ae02af2d265d48d1fa0bd948217215401a41acff4","clm_72b06c24e0f4a56797a3f1bd8e0e1589b98d7c34e9000f89a1c1714bd239a5fa","clm_75f6254c08b372942de2c68bb5b36429cb3889e0702246025a87d606ae2d89fc","clm_802ca562c52decf5f6155c4b3b52df561ea956d672a7b2205962c5aec10351fe","clm_bcfb9b614523b974f2dc868d667ecd693f46fa6660ac174d75cde8ed6334078c","clm_eb9b3d058152902a155c12a496f1b71be8082f6ae154e12501d250edcf0aa543","clm_f3c7c5b3e09dce8e228ddd65d370a6c1f9e3aaf2ad8139393c5482b1f24fc103","clm_fabbbf3f4b19050237a43e34da3c6ffe92e35dba3c9f299ca5e1ec2c4331fb3e","clm_fd5514cb5bb578c53202434fd7f5d4a9fd1f940ecfd2d9489b350c8335be030b"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:30:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_fc7daaf917a34b80b4790f6c97eb113e","id":"pg_65ce2fe2258d557190b427a0724489cd","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/patched-codes-patchwork-readme-md-21948cbec44d-27a0724489cd.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_40d8d0bdab2757c6bb5b492295d90375"],"title":"patched-codes/patchwork/README.md @ 21948cbec44d","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:30:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fc7daaf917a34b80b4790f6c97eb113e"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_07daf6fe71596bbf02fc228171e184fba93674dac7c8c42651c58df96c3c9020"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: building from source uses Poetry, with documented steps to install Poetry, clone the repository, activate a poetry shell, and run 'poetry install --all-extras'."}],"claim_ids":["clm_07daf6fe71596bbf02fc228171e184fba93674dac7c8c42651c58df96c3c9020"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:30:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_fc7daaf917a34b80b4790f6c97eb113e","id":"pg_a436caa4ca8e531f89f0ea1f70c74e56","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/patched-codes-patchwork-install-md-21948cbec44d-ea1f70c74e56.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_70c9e173c78d52cf843acce45e47323b"],"title":"patched-codes/patchwork/INSTALL.md @ 21948cbec44d","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:30:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fc7daaf917a34b80b4790f6c97eb113e"}
